  "chapter": 538,
  "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
  "text": " \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 13 Chapter 538\n \n        MEMORANDUM filed with Senate Bill Number 5935, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to  amend  the  judiciary law, in relation to enacting the\n        'hope card act'\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This bill would require the Office of Court Administration to  develop\na program to provide protected parties with a wallet-sized document that\ncontains  key information from the final order of protection and has the\nsame legal validity as a copy of the  order  itself.  This  \"hope  card\"\nwould  provide  survivors  of domestic violence with an effective way to\nprovide information about the protective order and about the perpetrator\nso that law enforcement and other entities can help keep these  individ-\nuals safe.\n\n  I  wholeheartedly  support  this  legislation,  which  would  serve to\nprotect survivors from those who would seek to cause them harm. However,\nthe Office of Court Administration could more effectively implement  the\nlegislation with some technical amendments.\n \n  I  have  reached  an agreement with the Legislature to ensure that the\nOffice  of  Court  Administration  can  offer  an  electronic  order  of\nprotection  as  an additional option to the wallet-size durable card for\nprotected parties and to authorize the issuance of the  hope  cards  for\norders of protection issued by any state court. Based on that agreement,\nI am signing this legislation.\n \n  This bill is approved.                         (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2023
 },
